  "excluded": [
    {
      "test": "system.test.ts > system > system can be immediately accessed outside the actor",
      "reason": "reads actor.system.get('someChild') on a root created and not started, which the create and get steps now express, and XState finds the invoked child there, as its createActor constructs the root, and so its initial children, at once; xstate constructs the root only on the host's start, so before it the system holds none of the root's children: the difference \"The root is constructed on start\" (doc: #differences-construction). It would need xstate to construct the root when it is created"
    },
